Hi, thanks for taking a look.

Before trying the suggestions below, I configured the kernel as =
requested in your other reply: I disabled Xenomai debug and turned off =
the function tracer. I attached the new .config for reference.

On 2011-04-08, at 1:25 AM, Gilles Chanteperdrix wrote:

> Is there any way you could set up a serial console instead?

I'll try but odds aren't good. Sorry.

> Could you try running latency in text mode?

Sure. I get the same results as in desktop mode. See attached =
'textmode.kernel.log', a dump of dmesg immediately before running =
latency.

> If the latency test succeeds, how do the figures it prints look?
>=20
> Could you try
> latency -p 1000
> ?

With `sudo /usr/xenomai/bin/latency -p 1000` I get:
[sudo]
=3D=3D Sampling period: 1000 us
=3D=3D Test mode: periodic user-mode task
=3D=3D All results in microseconds
warming up...

Then the cursor stops blinking and there's no response to keyboard =
input. I've attached another kernel log, grabbed just before running the =
above, as 'textmode-opts.kernel.log'.

Thanks for taking a look.
-Nolan

